---
title: AniOS Memory - Manager Overview
---
flowchart TB
    User([You send a message])
    User --> Route[1. Decide which memory<br/>could help]
    Route --> Understand[2. Create one reusable<br/>meaning vector]
    Understand --> Retrieve[3. Retrieve permitted,<br/>relevant memories]
    Retrieve --> Curate[4. Rank, deduplicate<br/>and limit context]
    Curate --> Answer[5. Assistant answers<br/>memory is data, not instructions]
    Answer --> User

    subgraph Forms[Memory forms]
        Short[Short term<br/>LLM context window<br/>Session working memory<br/>Semantic cache]
        Long[Long term<br/>Procedural / workflow · Toolbox · Entity<br/>Knowledge base · Persona · Semantic<br/>Episodic · Summaries · Conversations]
    end
    Retrieve -. reads .-> Short
    Retrieve -. reads .-> Long

    Answer -. may propose .-> Consent{Save something new?}
    Consent -->|only after approval| Long

    Control[Inspect short-term state<br/>View, correct, export or delete durable memory]
    Short --- Control
    Long --- Control

    classDef person fill:#e8f1fb,stroke:#5e8fc4,color:#102a43;
    classDef step fill:#f5f5f7,stroke:#86868b,color:#1d1d1f;
    classDef gate fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#b78b20,color:#4d3900;
    classDef store fill:#eef7ee,stroke:#5f9562,color:#183b1b;
    classDef note fill:#f1edff,stroke:#8872c6,color:#2e2450;
    class User person;
    class Route,Understand,Retrieve,Curate,Answer step;
    class Consent gate;
    class Short,Long store;
    class Control note;
